      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EEnglish Housewifry\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Elizabeth Moxon, 1764 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#moxon-1764\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EMoxon 1764\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003E11. To make POVERADE.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake a pint of good gravy, half a jill of elder vinegar, six shalots, a little pepper and salt, boil all these together a few minutes, and strain it off. This is a proper sauce for turkey, or any other sort of white fowls.\u003Cbr\u003E"
